red statements, logged batches, and server-reported query errors against driver 3.11.5, driver 4.3.1, and Apache driver 4.19.3.\n\nThe Java agent covers all three driver lines. The published `opentelemetry-cassandra-4.4` library instrumentation runs against Apache driver 4.19.3. Earlier driver lines remain agent-only because OpenTelemetry does not publish standalone instrumentation for them.\n\nScenario contracts can now declare `allowed_metrics` alongside required `metrics`. Cassandra uses this to require `db.client.operation.duration` while accepting optional Java SDK and exporter self-metrics.\n","title":"Add Java Cassandra database conformance"},"mode":"publish","pr":135,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1791844373,"generation":3,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"5337b0903ac64fbda3f783a1cf876b90","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":["Analyze (actions)","CodeQL","Coverage model","Discover scenarios","EasyCLA","Lint","Relock (${{ matrix.ecosystem }})","Scenarios (database-java)","Scenarios (gen-ai-python)","Scenarios (http-dotnet)","Scenarios (http-go)","Scenarios (http-java)","Scenarios (http-js)","Scenarios (http-php)","Scenarios (http-python)","Scenarios (http-ruby-net_http-opentelemetry-instrumentation-net_http-client)","Scenarios (http-ruby-rack-opentelemetry-instrumentation-rack-server)","Test (ubuntu-latest, Python 3.14)","Test (windows-latest, Python 3.14)","Types","Zizmor Security Analysis / Zizmor Security Analysis","required-status-check","zizmor"]},"repo":"open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-conformance","repo_id":1324141285,"request_id":"1300595adec34bad855d549a07996b58","schema":2,"source_private":false,"target_private":false,"workflow_ref":"review-loop-revisions/5d6ad62b673c0c9d4746d35b84ef1beb64efd265","workflow_revision":"5d6ad62b673c0c9d4746d35b84ef1beb64efd265"},"run":{"attempt":1,"conclusion":"success","id":38317643988,"url":"https://github.com/trask/copi